module

public import Theory.Mathieu.M23.Properties.Simplicity
public import Theory.GroupTheory.WordSubgroup

/-!
# Finite permutation data for M23 involution fusion

The three displayed permutations generate a subgroup with 128 elements.
The tables record its elements, generator transitions, and short words.
Conjugating words in the already certified M22 generators and the 23-cycle
send the first M22 generator to each of the 35 involutions in this list.
All identities and design membership certificates are checked by the kernel;
the GAP/Python enumeration used to find the data is not a proof dependency.

This supplies the finite computation for the M23 involution assertion used in
Aschbacher--Smith, *The Classification of Quasithin Groups*, Lemma 5.2.21
(printed p.657). The exhaustive Sylow argument is in the parent module.
-/

namespace Sporadic.Mathieu.M23Geometry.FusionCertificate

